ly 8 behind."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "The 20k's H8 lost 9.1 points, the biggest slip of the game, and moved Black's lead from -9.0 to +0.1. The engine's choice was D2. This was the one moment Black was ahead."}, {"turn": 33, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol answered with D5, losing 8.2 points and dropping from +0.1 to -8.1. The engine also preferred D2 here. The lead lasted exactly one move, and Black never had it again."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "D3 lost 3.9 points, taking the lead from -12.2 to -16.1, the lowest it reached. The engine preferred B2. The 20k then lost 2.3, 4.0 and 4.1 on the following White moves and let the gap shrink to the final 10.0. Black ended up holding the whole left side, but it was too late to catch up."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script only parsed the returned board (the inspect19 group/liberty/region inventory), counted current area, wrapped mcp__go__play with logging, converted moves to SGF, and read or wrote notes and records. None of it ranks candidate moves or looks ahead, so the player chose every move itself.", "stop": false}}